From 47070f955499fdcefe15eadf7be0c4204c5ec8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2025 16:03:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 682/913] plat-stm32mp1: fix return value of low power
 functions for STM32MP15

Fix the return value of enter_cstop_suspend and __psci_system_suspend
when CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM is not activated for STM32MP15.

This patch avoids to answer a error on PSCI system suspend request when
the Standby/cpu pwr down request is not really performed but change for
hardware restriction to Stop mode and simple WFI (for example when
Cortext-M4 not allows Standby mode with the bit PPDS in PWR_MCUCR).

The behavior is identical for CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM activated.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git f69d4875faffb1821193265f7a4ead6034705ccb plat-stm32mp1: fix return value of low power functions for STM32MP15]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I1535afa2226040b1c8ec2dec2074ff4939c881f3
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/494619
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
index 1db5e5045..ab862d759 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
@@ -243,8 +243,8 @@ static int enter_cstop_suspend(unsigned int soc_mode)
 	stm32_enter_cstop(soc_mode);
 
 #ifndef CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM
-	stm32mp_pm_call_bl2_lp_entry(soc_mode);
-	rc = 0;
+	if (stm32mp_pm_call_bl2_lp_entry(soc_mode) == TEE_SUCCESS)
+		rc = 0;
 #else
 	if (need_to_backup_cpu_context(soc_mode)) {
 		stm32_pm_cpu_power_down_wfi();
@@ -387,6 +387,18 @@ uint32_t __weak __psci_system_suspend(uintptr_t entry,
 			if (!IS_ENABLED(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND))
 				sm_restore_unbanked_regs(&nsec->ub_regs);
 		}
+#ifndef CFG_STM32MP1_OPTEE_IN_SYSRAM
+		/*
+		 * TF-A return to caller if standby is aborted (error)
+		 * or is reduced to Stop mode with simple WFI exit
+		 * so result OK as low power mode is performed (Stop)
+		 * PS: for OPTEE in SYSRAM and aborted Standby,
+		 *     stm32_pm_cpu_power_down_wfi() calls
+		 *     stm32mp_sysram_resume()
+		 *     and this part is NOT reached
+		 */
+		ret = 0;
+#endif
 	} else {
 		ret = plat_suspend((uint32_t)soc_mode);
 	}
-- 
